 "title": "One formula for the growth of rings of knots",
 "claim": "For an odd ring of n >= 5 knots with j spare distinctions, the (v, S) model's per-round count c(t) = sum_v C(m(v), t - h(v)) satisfies c(t) = sum_i C(j, i) c(t - n - i) after a transient (Vandermonde), rate the unique root above 1 of x^(n+j) = (1+x)^j; with a spare at every knot, c(t) = n F(t+2) for every t. Rings of three, four and six degenerate (one group of three; two common neighbours; two triples). The identification with the growth as in RING-GROWTH-20261118-001A, checked on 17 rings.",
